{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Data Movements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to explain data movement"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Implement data migration processes and data backups within the IT solution.  Understand the different types of data movements, making an emphasis on data migration movements as well as data backups"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on software testing, test estimation, and data migration processes"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verbs for speculating  Negative Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are <span class=\"strong\">Modal Verbs</span> used to make assumptions about something you don't know is happening or not."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English language, there are verbs with different functions depending on the context and tense they are used. In this case, we use the <strong>modal verbs express speculation</strong> to talk about something that is likely to happen. </br></br>  They can be used in negative statements as well expressing the idea in a more skeptical way. For example, if your friend did not come to work, you could think he or she is sick, but another friend doesn't think that because he or she considers your friend as a very healthy person. In such situation, a modal in negative may express disagreement and skepticism. </br></br>  Modal verbs are <strong>could</strong>, <strong>may</strong>, <strong>might</strong>, <strong>must</strong>, and <strong>will</strong>. </br></br>  The structure that we follow to use these <strong>modals of speculation</strong> in the <strong>negative form</strong> is this: </br></br>  Subject + <strong>modal verb</strong> + <strong>not</strong> + verb + complement</br></br>  Remember that you can use the contracted form of some verbs plus the negative particle: </br></br>  Could not \u2013 Couldn't Must not \u2013 Mustn't Will not \u2013 Won't</br></br>   Examples: </br></br>  <i>Anna <strong>couldn't</strong> be sick. I saw him yesterday, and she looked perfect. </br> These data <strong>may not</strong> work properly for our tasks; let's use other database. </br> Jonah didn't come to work. He <strong>might be</strong> sick. </br> Our work <strong>won't</strong> be efficient if we don't get the appropriate data.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Moving data might not be easy but being prepared is something that totally pays off. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "People can't trust only on the fact that they're doing their jobs well; it is necessary to have sort of a backup. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Data Movements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different types of<span class=\"strong\"> Data Movement</span> that may fit different types of data and different requests. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Data movement implies manipulation of invaluable information and thus, such manipulation should be done under controlled conditions to avoid data loss. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The main types of data movement are:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Consolidation </span> where data coming from different sources is collected and conveyed in a single destination. It allows having a full inventory of information under one system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Migration</span> which is done when data needs to be moved from one source to another.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Upgrade </span> is done when new software or a new version of the system is about to be installed, and information needs to be placed in the new system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Integration </span>which implies the combination and consolidation of data from a variety of sources under a sole data system, this allows people to access information more easily and faster. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "must have "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something so necessary it can't be overlooked "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Data migration is a very important must have in every company or project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "put something together "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to assemble or gather something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Consolidation may not be the most popular, but it is the one in charge of collecting data coming from different sources and putting all together in a single point or destination."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upgrading "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the action of getting or installing a better version of software "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Upgrading, instead, is the data movement people perform when setting up a newer version of software."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "favor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give a benefit or advantage "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also favors the management of true information\u2026."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ease "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to facilitate or make easier "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:It also favors the management of true information under one base which eases any kind of transaction or process that requires verification."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "squander "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to waste or not to fully take advantage  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: : Finally, a proper use of information makes people work better by not squandering time and resources wondering or panicking when something goes wrong."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about data migration process. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write information about how often is it advisable carried out, and how is it?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a process which you show the process and the variables to carry out."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information with your instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " look for more information about data migration process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write information about how do it and  how often"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the data migration process and talk about it."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "Data migration is a very important must have for every company or project. Moving data allows users to apply changes or transfer information from one system to another, like to a storage or database. It is usually done when updating or changing software, or when different systems need to be merged in one. Moving data might not be easy but being prepared is something that totally pays off. People can't trust only on the fact that they're doing their jobs well; it is necessary to have sort of a backup."}, {"time": "31000", "image": "enpe8n6le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "There are different types of data movement that imply different processes and sources. Consolidation may not be the most popular, but it is the one in charge of collecting data coming from different sources and putting all together in a single point or destination. Migration, which is the most used, implies moving data from one source to another. Upgrading, instead, is the data movement people perform when setting up a newer version of software. The last one is integration, which consists of the combination or consolidation of data from different sources under a unique data system, allowing a unified view of the information."}, {"time": "67500", "image": "enpe8n6le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Migration prevents the loss of data that might be essential for companies or project development. In the same way, data movement prevents fraud when done properly, especially in institutions where personal information is handled. It also favors the management of true information under one base which eases any kind of transaction or process that requires verification. Finally, a proper use of information makes people work better by not squandering time and resources wondering or panicking when something goes wrong."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le03ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe the different types of data movement. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain what data migration is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the importance of data migration."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever lost valuable information that you couldn't get back? If so, how did you lose it? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How many ways to store information do you know? Describe them."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Ways of Dealing with Data"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Listen to the following introduction to data movement"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "c